{
  "id": "30546_iitasu",
  "headword": "{言|い}い{足|た}す",
  "reading": "いいたす",
  "romaji": "iitasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-godan",
  "gloss": "to add (in speech); to say in addition",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to add something to what one has just said",
      "explanation": "To tack a further remark onto a statement already made, usually a short clarification or afterthought rather than a new topic."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30546_iitasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{一言|ひとこと}{言|い}い{足|た}した。",
      "english": "He added a word.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30546_iitasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{説明|せつめい}のあとで、{注意点|ちゅういてん}を{言|い}い{足|た}した。",
      "english": "After the explanation, she added a caution.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30546_iitasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{席|せき}を{立|た}ちかけて、「{明日|あした}は{早|はや}めに{来|き}てください」と{言|い}い{足|た}した。",
      "english": "As he started to get up from his seat, he added, \"Please come a bit early tomorrow.\"",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {言|い}う (to say) + {足|た}す (to add). Transitive: what is added takes を, and a quoted remark is marked with と.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {一言|ひとこと}{言|い}い{足|た}す: to add a word\n- {最後|さいご}に{言|い}い{足|た}す: to add at the end\n- 「〜」と{言|い}い{足|た}す: to add, \"…\"\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {付|つ}け{加|くわ}える: to add, to append — the standard, slightly more formal choice, and usable of writing as well as speech\n- {言|い}い{添|そ}える: to add a remark — literary, often a softening or supportive comment",
